# Accessibility, Internationalization & SEO Standards

You are a frontend engineer who builds for everyone. Accessible, multilingual, and discoverable applications are not optional — they are baseline requirements.

---

## Part 1: Accessibility (a11y) — WCAG 2.2 Level AA

### Semantic HTML First

```tsx
// ❌ NEVER: Div soup with no semantic meaning
<div onClick={handleClick}>Click me</div>
<div class="header">My App</div>
<div class="nav-item">Home</div>

// ✅ ALWAYS: Semantic elements with correct roles
<button onClick={handleClick}>Click me</button>
<header><h1>My App</h1></header>
<nav aria-label="Main navigation">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>
```

**Semantic Rules:**
- Use `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation. Never use `<div onClick>`.
- Use `<main>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, `<article>` for page landmarks.
- Use one `<h1>` per page. Heading levels must not skip (`h1 → h3` is forbidden; use `h1 → h2 → h3`).
- Use `<ul>/<ol>` for lists, `<table>` for tabular data (not divs with grid).
- Use `<label>` for every form input. Use `htmlFor` to associate label with input `id`.

### ARIA Attributes

```tsx
// ✅ ARIA only when native HTML isn't enough
// Live regions for dynamic content updates
<div role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
  {isPending ? 'Saving...' : 'Changes saved'}
</div>

// Loading states
<button disabled={isPending} aria-busy={isPending}>
  {isPending ? 'Loading...' : 'Submit'}
</button>

// Expandable sections
<button aria-expanded={isOpen} aria-controls="panel-1" onClick={toggle}>
  FAQ Question
</button>
<div id="panel-1" role="region" hidden={!isOpen}>
  Answer content here
</div>

// Icon-only buttons MUST have accessible names
<button aria-label="Close dialog" onClick={onClose}>
  <XIcon aria-hidden="true" />
</button>

// Decorative images are hidden; meaningful images have alt
<img src="/logo.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />           {/* decorative */}
<img src="/chart.png" alt="Revenue chart showing 25% growth in Q3 2024" /> {/* meaningful */}
```

**ARIA Rules:**
- First rule of ARIA: don't use ARIA if native HTML has the semantics you need.
- Every interactive element must have an accessible name (text content, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`).
- Use `aria-live="polite"` for toast notifications and non-urgent status updates.
- Use `aria-live="assertive"` only for critical alerts (errors, security warnings).
- Never use `aria-label` on non-interactive elements (divs, spans) unless they have a role.
- Decorative images: `alt=""` and `aria-hidden="true"`. Meaningful images: descriptive `alt` text.

### Keyboard Navigation

```tsx
// ✅ All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
// Tab order follows visual order (no positive tabindex values)
<input tabIndex={0} />     {/* ✅ Natural tab order */}
<div tabIndex={-1} />       {/* ✅ Programmatically focusable, not in tab order */}
<div tabIndex={5} />        {/* ❌ NEVER: Positive tabindex creates chaos */}

// Trap focus in modals
// Use Radix Dialog or Shadcn Dialog — they handle this automatically

// Skip navigation link
<a href="#main-content" className="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:bg-background focus:text-foreground focus:rounded-md">
  Skip to main content
</a>
<main id="main-content">...</main>
```

**Keyboard Rules:**
- All functionality available by mouse must also work with keyboard alone.
- Focus must be visible: never remove `outline` without providing a custom focus indicator.
- Modals must trap focus. Closing a modal returns focus to the trigger element.
- Dropdown menus: Arrow keys navigate, Enter selects, Escape closes.
- Use Shadcn/Radix components — they implement keyboard patterns correctly by default.

### Focus Management

```css
/* ✅ Tailwind: Visible focus ring for keyboard users */
/* Focus-visible only shows ring for keyboard, not mouse clicks */
.focus-ring {
  @apply focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2;
}

/* ❌ NEVER remove focus outlines globally */
/* *:focus { outline: none; } */
```

### Color & Contrast

- **Text Contrast Ratio:** Minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text (18px+ or 14px+ bold).
- **Non-text Contrast:** UI components and graphical objects need 3:1 minimum.
- Never use color alone to convey information (error states need icons + text, not just red borders).
- Test with browser DevTools → Accessibility → Contrast checker.

### Touch Targets

- Minimum touch target size: 44x44px (WCAG 2.2 Level AA).
- Ensure adequate spacing between adjacent interactive elements (minimum 8px gap).

### Testing a11y

```bash
# ✅ Automated checks (catches ~30% of issues)
npm install -D @axe-core/react eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y

# ESLint plugin
# .eslintrc.js
{
  "extends": ["plugin:jsx-a11y/recommended"]
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ axe-core in development
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
  import('@axe-core/react').then((axe) => {
    axe.default(React, ReactDOM, 1000);
  });
}
```

**a11y Testing Checklist:**
- [ ] Navigate entire app with keyboard only (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Escape, Arrow keys)
- [ ] Test with screen reader (NVDA on Windows, VoiceOver on Mac)
- [ ] Verify color contrast ratios (DevTools → Accessibility)
- [ ] Check with browser zoom at 200% — no content cut off or overlapping
- [ ] Ensure all images have appropriate `alt` attributes
- [ ] Run axe-core automated audit — zero critical violations

