## Part 2: Internationalization (i18n)

### Setup with next-intl (Recommended for Next.js)

```bash
npm install next-intl
```

```typescript
// messages/en.json
{
  "common": {
    "welcome": "Welcome, {name}!",
    "items": "You have {count, plural, =0 {no items} one {# item} other {# items}}.",
    "save": "Save",
    "cancel": "Cancel",
    "loading": "Loading...",
    "error": "Something went wrong"
  },
  "auth": {
    "login": "Sign in",
    "logout": "Sign out",
    "email": "Email address",
    "password": "Password"
  }
}

// messages/id.json
{
  "common": {
    "welcome": "Selamat datang, {name}!",
    "items": "Anda memiliki {count, plural, =0 {tidak ada item} other {# item}}.",
    "save": "Simpan",
    "cancel": "Batal",
    "loading": "Memuat...",
    "error": "Terjadi kesalahan"
  },
  "auth": {
    "login": "Masuk",
    "logout": "Keluar",
    "email": "Alamat email",
    "password": "Kata sandi"
  }
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ Usage in components
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';

export function Dashboard({ userName, itemCount }: Props) {
  const t = useTranslations('common');

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>{t('welcome', { name: userName })}</h1>
      <p>{t('items', { count: itemCount })}</p>
      <button>{t('save')}</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**i18n Rules:**
- Never hardcode user-facing strings. Always use translation keys.
- Support RTL (right-to-left) layouts for Arabic, Hebrew, etc. Use `dir="rtl"` and logical CSS properties (`margin-inline-start` instead of `margin-left`).
- Format dates, numbers, and currencies with `Intl.DateTimeFormat` / `Intl.NumberFormat` — never manual string formatting.
- Use ICU message format for pluralization — it handles complex plural rules per locale.
- Keep translation keys organized by feature/page namespace.
- Fallback locale: always define a fallback (usually English) for missing translations.

```tsx
// ✅ Date & number formatting with Intl API
const formattedDate = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale, {
  year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric'
}).format(new Date());

const formattedPrice = new Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {
  style: 'currency', currency: 'USD'
}).format(29.99);
```

