## Part 3: SEO (Search Engine Optimization)

### Metadata API (Next.js 15)

```typescript
// ✅ Static metadata — app/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Home | YourApp',
  description: 'Build amazing products with our platform. Start free today.',
  keywords: ['saas', 'productivity', 'project management'],
  authors: [{ name: 'Your Name' }],
  creator: 'YourApp',
  openGraph: {
    type: 'website',
    locale: 'en_US',
    url: 'https://yourapp.com',
    siteName: 'YourApp',
    title: 'YourApp — Build Amazing Products',
    description: 'Build amazing products with our platform.',
    images: [{ url: '/og-image.png', width: 1200, height: 630, alt: 'YourApp Preview' }],
  },
  twitter: {
    card: 'summary_large_image',
    title: 'YourApp — Build Amazing Products',
    description: 'Build amazing products with our platform.',
    images: ['/og-image.png'],
  },
  robots: {
    index: true,
    follow: true,
    googleBot: { index: true, follow: true, 'max-image-preview': 'large' },
  },
  alternates: {
    canonical: 'https://yourapp.com',
    languages: { 'en': '/en', 'id': '/id' },
  },
};
```

```typescript
// ✅ Dynamic metadata — app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';

type Props = { params: Promise<{ slug: string }> };

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const post = await getPost(slug);

  if (!post) return { title: 'Post Not Found' };

  return {
    title: `${post.title} | Blog`,
    description: post.excerpt,
    openGraph: {
      title: post.title,
      description: post.excerpt,
      type: 'article',
      publishedTime: post.publishedAt.toISOString(),
      authors: [post.author.name],
      images: [{ url: post.coverImage, width: 1200, height: 630 }],
    },
  };
}
```

### Structured Data (JSON-LD)

```tsx
// ✅ JSON-LD for rich search results
export default function ProductPage({ product }: { product: Product }) {
  const jsonLd = {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Product',
    name: product.name,
    description: product.description,
    image: product.images,
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      price: product.price,
      priceCurrency: 'USD',
      availability: product.inStock
        ? 'https://schema.org/InStock'
        : 'https://schema.org/OutOfStock',
    },
    aggregateRating: {
      '@type': 'AggregateRating',
      ratingValue: product.rating,
      reviewCount: product.reviewCount,
    },
  };

  return (
    <>
      <script type="application/ld+json" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: JSON.stringify(jsonLd) }} />
      {/* Page content */}
    </>
  );
}
```

### Technical SEO

```tsx
// ✅ app/sitemap.ts — Auto-generated sitemap
import type { MetadataRoute } from 'next';

export default async function sitemap(): Promise<MetadataRoute.Sitemap> {
  const posts = await getAllPosts();

  const postEntries = posts.map((post) => ({
    url: `https://yourapp.com/blog/${post.slug}`,
    lastModified: post.updatedAt,
    changeFrequency: 'weekly' as const,
    priority: 0.7,
  }));

  return [
    { url: 'https://yourapp.com', lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'daily', priority: 1.0 },
    { url: 'https://yourapp.com/about', lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'monthly', priority: 0.5 },
    { url: 'https://yourapp.com/pricing', lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'weekly', priority: 0.8 },
    ...postEntries,
  ];
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ app/robots.ts
import type { MetadataRoute } from 'next';

export default function robots(): MetadataRoute.Robots {
  return {
    rules: [
      { userAgent: '*', allow: '/', disallow: ['/api/', '/admin/', '/dashboard/'] },
    ],
    sitemap: 'https://yourapp.com/sitemap.xml',
  };
}
```

**SEO Rules:**
- Every page must have a unique `<title>` (50-60 chars) and `meta description` (150-160 chars).
- Use one `<h1>` per page. The `<h1>` should match or closely relate to the page `<title>`.
- All images: descriptive `alt` text (except decorative images).
- Set `canonical` URLs to prevent duplicate content issues.
- Implement Open Graph and Twitter Card meta tags for social sharing.
- Use `next/image` for automatic image optimization and lazy loading.
- Generate `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt` programmatically.
- Implement JSON-LD structured data for rich search results.
- Ensure pages are server-rendered or statically generated (not client-only SPA) for crawlability.

### SEO Checklist

- [ ] Unique `<title>` and `<meta description>` on every page
- [ ] One `<h1>` per page with proper heading hierarchy
- [ ] All meaningful images have descriptive `alt` text
- [ ] Open Graph + Twitter Card meta tags set
- [ ] `sitemap.xml` auto-generated and submitted to Google Search Console
- [ ] `robots.txt` configured (block `/api/`, `/admin/`)
- [ ] Canonical URLs set on all pages
- [ ] JSON-LD structured data on product/article pages
- [ ] Server-rendered or statically generated (not client-only)
- [ ] Core Web Vitals passing (LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1)
